<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="db4abde3">&lt;p&gt;
    Leverages an understanding of the technology landscape along with knowledge of organizational functions (HR, Finance
    &amp; Accounting, Procurement, etc.) to provide functional leadership through all phases of an engagement or project.
    Understands client requirements at a macro level and translates those requirements by defining the business
    capabilities to support the business functions. Aligns those business capabilities to business processes and identifies
    technology solutions to support them.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p/&gt;&lt;p&gt;
    The Functional Architect is typically responsible for:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Leading to-be business process workshops with the client
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Brokering compromise between solution design and operational strategy to minimize custom development
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Mapping business requirements to process flows
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identifying and documenting project-specific processes and functional gaps
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Managing execution of unit, integration and user acceptance testing
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reporting functional area progress to the Solution Architect
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
